## SourceUnitOwnershipV1
{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["schemaVersion","enumeration","units","selectedUnitIds","ownership"],"description":"The committed relation from a SNAPSHOT SOURCE PATH to the compilation TARGET that reads it, the closed table of those targets, and the EXPLICIT SELECTION of which of them this universe analyses. It exists because a body span dialect is a property of the compilation target: neither a crate-name-to-root map nor the package edition map can supply it, since #[path], files shared by several targets and several compilation contexts of one crate defeat a directory inference, and Cargo lets a target override its package default edition. Because this record is committed by H identity inside RustUniverseV2ResolvedInputs.sourceUnitOwnershipId, a different SELECTION is a different record, a different identity and therefore a DIFFERENT sourceUniverse: one physical source path compiled by two targets at two editions is validly analysed under each, one selection at a time, with no change to any relation payload. Every row is a retained native observation; nothing here executes Cargo, a build script or a repository read, and nothing here qualifies a compiler or an enumerator.","properties":{"schemaVersion":{"const":1},"enumeration":{"type":"string","enum":["complete","partial"],"description":"complete: every compiled source path OF THE SELECTED UNITS has a row, so a path with no row is not compiled by any selected target. partial: the producer did not finish, so an owner INSIDE the selected scope may exist that is not listed. These are different claims and the second is not a weaker form of the first: an unlisted owner could contradict a listed one, so no clone body dialect is admissible under partial. That is checked BEFORE any row lookup, so partial discovery can never act as an implicit edition selection by hiding a conflicting owner. Partial evidence remains useful under the existing facts and Coverage law: the clones scope reports its incompleteness and the predicate is indeterminate, rather than a body identity being minted on an unbounded claim."},"units":{"type":"array","maxItems":65536,"uniqueItems":true,"x-opensip-order":{"by":["unitId"]},"description":"The closed table of compilation targets. Strictly unique by unitId, and unitId is a FUNCTION of the metadata, so two contradictory rows for one purported unit are a refusal rather than two units that differ by accident. A selection or an ownership row naming a unitId with no row here is an unbound caller label and is inadmissible.","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["unitId","markerPath","crateName","targetKind","targetName","targetEdition"],"properties":{"unitId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}(?![\\s\\S])","x-opensip-digest":{"representation":"h-identity","domain":"native.compilation-unit.v1","form":"sha256-text","retention":"derived","authority":"native"},"description":"H(native.compilation-unit.v1, UnitIdentityV1{schemaVersion:1, markerPath, targetKind, targetName}) over the very fields this row carries. DERIVED retention: nothing separate is retained because the preimage IS the row, and admission re-derives and compares (sourceUnitOwnership.unitId). Not an opaque digest - preimage record, domain and selector are all published - and not a delimiter label, which could stay injective only by narrowing admitted repository paths."},"markerPath":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"pattern":"^(?!/)(?!.*(^|/)\\.\\.?(/|$))[^\\u0000\\\\]+(?![\\s\\S])","description":"The inventoried manifest that declares this target: the same markerPath vocabulary WorkspaceUnitV2 already uses, cited rather than duplicated. WorkspaceUnitV2 and UnitMembershipV1 identify WORKSPACE units - cargo-package and cargo-workspace - which is the wrong granularity here, because one package holds several targets that may carry different editions; naming the marker joins the two rather than competing with them."},"crateName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+(?![\\s\\S])","description":"A key of the universe edition map, which supplies the package default."},"targetKind":{"type":"string","enum":["lib","bin","test","bench","example","build-script"]},"targetName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+(?![\\s\\S])"},"targetEdition":{"oneOf":[{"type":"null"},{"type":"integer","enum":[2015,2018,2021,2024]}],"description":"The target's OWN edition when it sets one, null when it takes the package default. Cargo documents edition on a target as well as on a package: cargo-metadata lists targets[].edition and states the package edition is a DEFAULT individual targets may differ from. null DEFERS to the universe edition map for crateName, so the two committed places can never contradict: an override is explicit and visible, and its absence is explicit too."}}}},"selectedUnitIds":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":65536,"uniqueItems":true,"x-opensip-order":"utf8","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}(?![\\s\\S])","x-opensip-digest":{"representation":"h-identity","domain":"native.compilation-unit.v1","form":"sha256-text","retention":"derived","authority":"native"}},"description":"The EXPLICIT analysis scope: the compilation targets this universe analyses. Every member must be a unitId of the units table. This is what makes a shared path representable at two editions without an ambiguous claim - two selections are two universes - and it is what distinguishes SELECTED SCOPE from INCOMPLETE ENUMERATION. An owner outside the selection is deliberately out of scope and its edition does not bear on a body; an unlisted owner INSIDE the selection is a gap in knowledge and refuses. Silently omitting a conflicting owner from the units table is not a selection: the omission is invisible, whereas a selection is committed in the identity."},"ownership":{"type":"array","maxItems":1000000,"uniqueItems":true,"x-opensip-order":{"by":["path","unitId"]},"description":"The pure relation. It carries no edition and no metadata, so it cannot contradict the units table.","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["path","unitId"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"pattern":"^(?!/)(?!.*(^|/)\\.\\.?(/|$))[^\\u0000\\\\]+(?![\\s\\S])"},"unitId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}(?![\\s\\S])","x-opensip-digest":{"representation":"h-identity","domain":"native.compilation-unit.v1","form":"sha256-text","retention":"derived","authority":"native"}}}}}}}
